What I'd do is the following: pass a `SkyFunction.Environment` here, create a `PathFragment` for the `DO_NOT_BUILD_HERE` file, then do

```
Root absoluteRoot = Root.absoluteRoot(rootedPath.getRoot().geFileSystem());
RootedPath doNotBuildPath = RootedPath.toRootedPath(absoluteRoot, <do not build path>);
FileValue doNotBuildValue = env.getValue(FileValue.key(doNotBuildPath));
if (env.valuesMissing()) { 
  // Make getPackageExistenceAndSubdirDeps() return null early
}

return doNoBuildValue.exists();
```

It's a bit of overkill, but why not do it properly? The ugly hack with the roots doesn't really matter because this code path will be hit very, very infrequently.

